no_default_statements_in_datasource: a hand-written :DEFAULT in a data
source is always wrong (the builder generates :DEFAULT itself), in any
casing. Both lines report on the keyword; the lowercase one also reports
keyword_uppercase. The script layout here is the style guide's
datasource_not_script_layout Bad example in shape, so the defaultless
names also report datasource_default_required.
-- input.ds --
:PARAMETERS sAisle, nLevel;
:DEFAULT sAisle, "A";
:default nLevel, 1;
:RETURN sAisle + LimsString(nLevel);
-- format --
:PARAMETERS sAisle, nLevel;
:DEFAULT sAisle, "A";
:DEFAULT nLevel, 1;

:RETURN sAisle + LimsString(nLevel);
-- diagnostics --
